component SkillInstaller {
  goal {
    Discover and install valid agent skills bundled with the selected Sigil CLI
    distribution.

    Support global and project destinations for compatible agent hosts without
    replacing unrelated content or consulting workspace configuration.
  }

  interface {
    SkillCatalog {
      listInstalledSkills(sourceDirectory?) returns the resolved source directory and
      sorted valid skill names
    }

    SkillInstallation {
      installSkills(options?) returns the selected scope, agents, source directory,
      and installed, updated, existing, or copied destination results

      scope defaults to global and accepts global or project

      agents default to codex, claude, opencode, and pi

      Codex, OpenCode, and Pi share .agents/skills for the selected scope

      Claude Code uses .claude/skills for the selected scope

      global scope resolves destinations from userHome

      project scope resolves destinations from targetRoot or the current working
      directory
    }

    SkillSourceDiscovery {
      resolveInstalledSkillsDirectory(moduleUrl?, executablePath?) returns the first
      available installation-relative skills directory

      sourceDirectory defaults to the directory resolved from the selected Sigil
      executable or source module

      returned installation paths are absolute host paths
    }
  }
}

expand SkillInstaller {
  state {
    SkillCatalog {
      installable skills are sorted immediate non-hidden directories containing
      SKILL.md in the selected source directory
    }

    SkillInstallation {
      each destination is absent, managed by Sigil, or an unmanaged conflict
    }
  }

  logic {
    SkillSourceDiscovery {
      Resolve skills beside the selected executable before considering source-module
      development fallbacks.

      Executable lookup checks executableDirectory/../integrations/skills before
      executableDirectory/integrations/skills.

      File-module fallback checks moduleDirectory/../integrations/skills before
      moduleDirectory/../../../integrations/skills.

      Deduplicate candidate paths, select the first existing directory, and report
      every checked path when none exists.

      A versioned layout resolves version/bin/sigil to version/integrations/skills.

      Source development may resolve the repository integrations/skills directory
      relative to installer.ts.
    }

    SkillCatalog {
      Discover only immediate non-hidden directories containing SKILL.md.

      Reject a missing source directory or one containing no valid skills.
    }

    SkillInstallation {
      Deduplicate destinations shared by Codex, OpenCode, and Pi.

      Preflight every destination before changing any managed installation.

      Prefer relative directory links and fall back to managed copies when permitted
      link creation fails.

      Record managed-installation metadata sufficient to distinguish Sigil-owned
      destinations.

      Retarget or replace an older Sigil-managed installation when the selected
      executable owns different skill assets.

      Refuse to replace an unmanaged destination.

      Create or update project-local skill .gitignore files with root-anchored
      entries for managed metadata and skills.

      Preserve unrelated ignore rules, newline style, and existing managed entries
      without duplication.

      Return destination records in stable skill and agent order.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    SkillCatalog {
      Skill names are discovered from integrations/skills and are not hardcoded into
      command logic.

      Hidden entries, files, source symlinks, and directories without SKILL.md are
      not valid skills.
    }

    SkillInstallation {
      Links use host-native relative targets.

      Directory symlink type is explicit for Windows when link creation is permitted.

      Path equality is case-insensitive on Windows and case-sensitive on macOS and
      Linux.

      An unmanaged file, directory, or symlink is never replaced.

      Conflict preflight completes before any managed destination changes.

      Project ignore entries cover generated links, copies, and management metadata
      while the ignore file remains repository content.

      The selected executable owns skill-source selection; installation does not
      inspect ConfigFile to choose or switch binaries.

      Filesystem and host permission failures propagate as CLI runtime failures.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    SkillInstallation {
      Decision: Protect user-owned destinations by preflighting every target and
      replacing only installations with Sigil management evidence.

      Scope: Governs installation and update ownership for selected skill
      destinations; excludes source discovery and link-versus-copy mechanics.

      Trade-offs: One unmanaged conflict aborts the complete installation instead of
      partially updating other targets.

      Consequences: Reinstallation can update managed destinations while unrelated
      files, directories, and links remain untouched.

      Revisit when: Agent hosts provide a shared transactional package-management
      authority.
    }
  }

  cases {
    SkillCatalog {
      A distribution containing multiple valid skills lists them in stable order
      without a CLI code change.

      An empty source directory reports a runtime failure.
    }

    SkillInstallation {
      Global installation creates one shared destination for Codex, OpenCode, and Pi
      and one Claude-compatible destination.

      Project installation creates equivalent destinations only inside the selected
      repository.

      A Windows host without directory-link permission receives a managed copy.

      Reinstalling from a different selected CLI updates older managed destinations.

      An unmanaged destination aborts installation before other destinations change.

      Repeating installation against current managed destinations reports existing
      and leaves project ignore files unchanged.
    }

    SkillSourceDiscovery {
      A selected version/bin/sigil resolves version-matched skill assets before
      source-module fallbacks.

      Two repositories invoking different selected binaries use the skill assets
      owned by their respective binaries.
    }
  }
}
